> A planar graph that needs unequal radii: K4

Four pairwise tangent equal positive disks cannot lie in the plane. Three
centres would form an equilateral triangle of side 2r; the only point equidistant
from all three is its circumcentre, at distance 2r/√3, rather than the required
2r. Thus an equal-radius restriction cannot represent all planar graphs by
tangency. This is a geometric obstruction, independent of iteration count.

K4 has a simple unequal-radius control. Put three unit disks at
(R,0), (−R/2,1), (−R/2,−1), where R=2/√3. Their pairwise distances are two.
A fourth disk at the origin with positive radius R−1 touches all three because
its centre distance R equals the sum of radii 1+(R−1). All six edges are
contacts with no interior overlaps. These explicit coordinates are a mathematical
control, not a new general-purpose packing algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/circle_k4_contacts.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1},{0,2},{0,3},{1,2},{1,3},{2,3}};
  const double radius=2/std::sqrt(3.0);
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::Circle2D> control{{{radius,0},1},{{-radius/2,1},1},{{-radius/2,-1},1},{{0,0},radius-1}};
  const auto native=dm::algorithms::circle_packing_layout(4,edges);
  dm::graphics::Diagram figure(95,1100);
  std::print("| K4 geometry | overlaps | edge contacts / 6 | extra contacts | zero radii | edge stress |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int panel=0;panel<2;++panel) {
    const auto& circles=panel?control:native;
    const auto m=dm::algorithms::circle_packing_metrics(circles,edges);const double shift=6.0*panel;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.9f} |\n",panel?"explicit unequal radii":"legacy returned disks",m.overlapping_pairs,m.edge_contacts,m.nonedge_contacts,m.zero_radii,m.edge_stress);
    if(panel && (m.edge_contacts!=6 || m.overlapping_pairs!=0 || m.zero_radii!=0))return 1;
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<circles.size();++i) {
      const auto& c=circles[i];
      figure.ellipse({c.center.x+shift,c.center.y},c.radius,c.radius,panel?dm::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::RGB{254,226,226})
            .text({c.center.x+shift,c.center.y},std::to_string(i),i==3 && panel?14:20);
    }
    figure.text({shift,3.3},panel?"explicit K4 packing\nthree unit disks + small disk":"legacy K4 drawing\nfour radii of 0.45",21)
          .text({shift,-3.3},std::format("{} of 6 edge contacts",m.edge_contacts),20);
  }
  figure.save_svg("build/circle_k4_contacts.svg");
}
