\caption(Unequal positive radii realize all six K4 contacts. The legacy drawing misses them, even though its disks are disjoint.)
\alttext(Four separate equal red disks are beside three large mutually tangent green disks surrounding a small green disk that touches all three. Vertex labels identify all four disks.)

The diagnostic tolerance is an absolute gap tolerance, default 1e−9. With
gap=d−r_i−r_j, overlap means gap<−tolerance, and contact means
|gap|≤tolerance. Counts may tolerate tiny overlaps; they do not certify an
exact-real packing. Edge stress sums squared edge gaps, and overlap penalty
sums squared negative gaps without tolerance clipping. Zero radii are counted
separately, while negative radii and nonfinite inputs reject.

> Checking the relaxation against a closed form

For the separated two-circle example, a sweep gives
d_(t+1)=(1−2η)d_t+4η. With η=0.08 and d_0=6,

$$
d_t=2+4(0.84)^t,\qquad
\Phi_t=\tfrac12(d_t-2)^2=8(0.84)^{2t}.
$$
\alttext(The two-circle distance error contracts by 0.84 per sweep, so its measured potential contracts by the square of that factor.)

This formula describes this symmetric two-vertex trajectory, not arbitrary
graphs. The next program compares captured energies directly to it. Ordinary
linear axes include the full measured energy range; there is no logarithmic
floor. After output normalization the two returned centres are always distance
two apart here, so the output gap stays 1.1 regardless of the raw improvement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/circle_energy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::algorithms::CirclePackingOptions options;options.iterations=30;options.snapshot_stride=1;
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::circle_packing_trace(2,{{0,1}},options);
  std::vector<double> iteration,measured,theory;
  std::print("| sweep | actual distance | measured energy | closed-form energy |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& frame:trace.frames) {
    const auto expected=8*std::pow(0.84L,2*frame.iteration);
    if(std::fabs(frame.energy-expected)>1e-10L)return 1;
    iteration.push_back(frame.iteration);measured.push_back(frame.energy);theory.push_back(expected);
    if(frame.iteration==0 || frame.iteration==1 || frame.iteration==5 || frame.iteration%10==0) {
      const auto a=frame.circles[0].center,b=frame.circles[1].center;
      std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n",frame.iteration,std::hypot(a.x-b.x,a.y-b.y),frame.energy,expected);
    }
  }
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.line(iteration,measured,"actual",{37,99,235},2)
      .points(iteration,theory,"closed form",{234,88,12},4)
      .legend({"actual captured energy","two-circle closed form"},{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}})
      .title("Measured pair energy agrees with its closed form")
      .x_label("completed simultaneous sweeps").y_label("raw pair potential")
      .x_limits(0,30).y_limits(0,8.5).save_svg("build/circle_energy.svg");
  options.iterations=1;options.step_size=2;
  const auto overshoot=dm::algorithms::circle_packing_trace(2,{{0,1}},options);
  std::print("\nAt step size 2, actual energy rises from {:.1f} to {:.1f}; returned gap remains {:.1f}.\n",overshoot.frames.front().energy,overshoot.frames.back().energy,overshoot.output_metrics.min_gap);
  if(overshoot.frames.back().energy<=overshoot.frames.front().energy)return 1;
}
