// result_end

For the symmetric eight-cycle, normalized neighbours are separated by
2sin(π/8), below the output diameter 0.9. Hence each adjacent returned pair
overlaps by about 0.134633135, even though this graph is planar. This is a
direct counterexample to a general non-overlap guarantee for the current output.

Canonical tests compare every simple graph through five vertices (1,100 graphs)
and 1,000 seeded random multigraph/control combinations with an independent
double-arithmetic Jacobi implementation. Closed forms check the two-circle and
triangle trajectories; the explicit K4 disks check positive-radius contacts.
Further cases cover duplicate/reversed edges, ignored loops, tolerance semantics,
snapshot ownership, exact/one-below caps, huge preflight counts, arithmetic range,
zero sweeps and zero step. All fourteen new cases pass address and undefined-
behaviour sanitizers. These checks establish the stated kernel and measurement
contracts, without claiming that arbitrary outputs solve a packing problem.

> What this analysis establishes

The native API now distinguishes actual raw relaxation from returned disks,
reports contact errors, and bounds requested pair work and recording. The
original triangle remains a deterministic drawing, with its missing tangencies
made visible. The K4 control explains why unequal radii matter; the eight-cycle
shows that returned overlaps are also possible. A true circle-packing solver
would require a different construction and its own correctness contract.

> References

- K. Stephenson (2005), *Introduction to Circle Packing: The Theory of Discrete
  Analytic Functions*, Cambridge University Press. The author's overview at
  https://www.circlepack.com/ describes prescribed tangencies and varying sizes.
  This is background for the geometric problem, not the algorithm implemented
  by datamunge's legacy equal-centre relaxation.
- Canonical implementation and contracts: include/datamunge/algorithms/circle_packing.hpp,
  src/datamunge/algorithms/circle_packing.cpp and the shared
  include/datamunge/algorithms/layout_geometry.hpp. The complete C++ programs
  above are the editable sources for every figure.
